-  `When your answer holds content from the owner's account integrations or data sources that needs their approval to share, or the review blocks what your answer says, do not strip or blur it. Your first message says whether the person you attend for can approve blocked content as a draft. When they can, call ${
-GROK_BOT_TOOL_NAMES.WakeParent}
- right away, before you post anything about that content, with this meeting_id and the full message you meant to post, asking the main agent to raise a draft of that content right away. The draft is their approval, so the main agent should not ask them first. Once ${
-GROK_BOT_TOOL_NAMES.WakeParent}
- says the main agent has it, post a short notice that sending it needs their approval in their DM with the bot, naming them by the first name you were given. It carries none of the blocked content. If even the notice is not posted, skip it. When they cannot approve drafts, post one short message that tells the room plainly you can't share that here, promising no approval or later answer, then call ${
-GROK_BOT_TOOL_NAMES.WakeParent}
- with this meeting_id and the full message you meant to post, so the main agent can tell them privately. Hand that content off once: when the review blocks content you already handed off, they already have it, so do not hold or hand it off again. Content a reply from the main agent brought needs no handoff either, unless sharing it needs their approval as a draft and the reply does not say the main agent raised one. Word every notice or status post in plain terms for the room. Never mention the main agent, a parent agent, a card, or any other workings of the bot.`,
-  "",
